<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span><span id="A4.F14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RM rank correlation on <span id="A4.F14.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OpinionQA</span></span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06391v1/prism_alignment_rms.png" id="A4.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/387;" width="476" height="387" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span><span id="A4.F15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alignment between RMs on <span id="A4.F15.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM</span>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F16" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06391v1/prism_spearman_rank_correlation.png" id="A4.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/416;" width="476" height="416" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 16: </span><span id="A4.F16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RM rank correlation on <span id="A4.F16.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM</span>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F17" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06391v1/opinion_qa_alignment.svg" id="A4.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/843;" width="476" height="843"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 17: </span><span id="A4.F17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alignment is largely dependent on model.</span> We visualize the alignment of RMs to the opinions of respondents in the <span id="A4.F17.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OpinionQA</span> dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span><span id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM</span></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ D.1 OpinionQA ‣ Appendix D RQ1 ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> shows the opinion alignment values on <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM</span>. Again, we verify using a Friedman test that the differences between the RM reward distributions are statistically significant, with a test statistic of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="295.73" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>295.73</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">295.73</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We show the alignment metric between RMs for the <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM</span> dataset in Figure <a href="#A4.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ D.1 OpinionQA ‣ Appendix D RQ1 ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A4.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ D.1 OpinionQA ‣ Appendix D RQ1 ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> showcases the Spearman’s rank correlation between the models on <span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM</span>. More granular rank correlations are listed in Table <a href="#A4.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ D.1 OpinionQA ‣ Appendix D RQ1 ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We display the same figures in Section <a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 RQ1: Whose opinions do models reward? ‣ 6 Whose opinions are rewarded? ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> for <span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM</span> in Figure <a href="#A4.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ D.2 PRISM ‣ Appendix D RQ1 ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F18" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06391v1/prism_demographics.svg" id="A4.F18.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/310;" width="476" height="310"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 18: </span><span id="A4.F18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM<span id="A4.F18.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> demographics alignment.</span></span> We show fine-grained alignment metrics on <span id="A4.F18.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PRISM</span> as in Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5 Determining reward model perspectives ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>RQ2</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span><span id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BBQ</span></h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F19" title="Figure 19 ‣ E.1 BBQ ‣ Appendix E RQ2 ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> is the rank complement to Figure <a href="#S6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 6.2 RQ2: Do models exhibit stereotypes? ‣ 6 Whose opinions are rewarded? ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F19" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06391v1/bbq_category_bias_rank.png" id="A5.F19.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:433/136;" width="433" height="136" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 19: </span><span id="A5.F19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stereotypes ranking (<math id="A5.F19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>) on <span id="A5.F19.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BBQ</span>.</span> We plot the rank of the proportion of correct labels by demographic group. The higher the percentage, the smaller the rank (i.e. an RM that predicted the label for a demographic group correctly <math id="A5.F19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math>% of the time would have rank <math id="A5.F19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>). This complements Figure <a href="#S6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 6.2 RQ2: Do models exhibit stereotypes? ‣ 6 Whose opinions are rewarded? ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> by visualizing the relative rate of stereotypes between demographic groups per RM.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span><span id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">StereoSet</span></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F20" title="Figure 20 ‣ E.2 StereoSet ‣ Appendix E RQ2 ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> is the rank complement to Figure <a href="#S6.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 6.2 RQ2: Do models exhibit stereotypes? ‣ 6 Whose opinions are rewarded? ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F20" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06391v1/stereoset_category_bias_rank.png" id="A5.F20.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/110;" width="476" height="110" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 20: </span><span id="A5.F20.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stereotypes ranking (<math id="A5.F20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>) on <span id="A5.F20.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">StereoSet</span>.</span> Within the predicted label <span id="A5.F20.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F1C0E8;">Stereotype</span>, we plot the rank of the percent of predicted labels for each demographic group. The lower the percentage, the smaller the rank (i.e. an RM that predicted the label <span id="A5.F20.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F1C0E8;">Stereotype</span> for a demographic group <math id="A5.F20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>% of the time would have rank <math id="A5.F20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>). This complements Figure <a href="#S6.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 6.2 RQ2: Do models exhibit stereotypes? ‣ 6 Whose opinions are rewarded? ‣ Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> by visualizing the relative rate of stereotypes between demographic groups per RM.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>RQ3</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
