<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 16: </span><span id="A6.T16.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">BBQ<span id="A6.T16.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> confusion matrix for </span>Beaver<span id="A6.T16.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> RM.</span></span> We remove refusals to reveal a clearer sense of the RM labels. For the entire dataset using <span id="A6.T16.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Beaver</span> RM, <math id="A6.T16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="49.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>49.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">49.7</annotation></semantics></math>% of <span id="A6.T16.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCFD2;">Stereotyped</span> responses are rewarded, and <math id="A6.T16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40.3</annotation></semantics></math>% of <span id="A6.T16.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-bg-color:#B9FBC0;">Unstereotyped</span> responses are rewarded.</figcaption>
