<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 17: </span><span id="A6.T17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">BBQ<span id="A6.T17.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> correctness by demographic on </span>Beaver<span id="A6.T17.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> RM.</span></span> We display the percentage of correct rewards (the label of the highest reward is the gold label) after refusals are removed. The differences across demographic groups are statistically significant using a <math id="A6.T17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-test, with <math id="A6.T17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}(47)=81.9,p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>47</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>81.9</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(47)=81.9,p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Effect size</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used the Wilcoxon signed-rank test instead of the more common Cohen’s <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, as the differences between steering and no steering were not normally distributed. We verify the non-normality of the distribution through the Shapiro-Wilk test, which yielded highly statistically significant (<math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>) results for <span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Bio</span> steering (<math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{SW}=0.877" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.877</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{SW}=0.877</annotation></semantics></math>), <span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Portray</span> steering (<math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{SW}=0.907" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.907</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{SW}=0.907</annotation></semantics></math>), and <span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">QA</span> steering (<math id="A6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{SW}=0.917" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.917</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{SW}=0.917</annotation></semantics></math>). The Wilcoxon effect size test yielded the test statistic <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{W}=2681201.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2681201.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{W}=2681201.0</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Bio</span> steering, <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{W}=2469142.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2469142.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{W}=2469142.0</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Portray</span> steering, and <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{W}=2758902.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2758902.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{W}=2758902.0</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">QA</span> steering. We employ a conservative two-tailed Wilcoxon signed-rank test.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Miscellaneous</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We ran our experiments on eight 10 GB NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 GPUs.</p>
</div>
</section><div class="ltx_rdf" about="" property="dcterms:title" content="Reward Model Perspectives: Whose Opinions Do Reward Models Reward?"></div>

</article>
